Overload resilience (laptop incident, 2026-11-11): a Windows backend notices its desktop launcher died
(Windows keeps the dead parent's id as ppid) and exits instead of holding the port and state lock, and a
refreshing query does not cancel and re-send a read still in flight on its interval.

